# Contributing to Component System
Guidelines for creating new components and maintaining existing ones.
## Creating New Components
### 1. Component Class
Location: `app/components/namespace/component_name_component.rb`
```ruby
class Namespace::ComponentNameComponent < ApplicationComponent
  def initialize(param:, variant: :default)
    @param = param
    @variant = variant
  end
  
  private
  
  attr_reader :param, :variant
  
  def variant_classes
    case variant
    when :primary then "bg-blue text-white"
    when :secondary then "bg-gray text-black"
    end
  end
end
```

### 2. Component Template
Location: `app/components/namespace/component_name_component.html.erb`

```erb
<div class="<%= variant_classes %>">
  <%= content %>
</div>
```
### 3. Lookbook Preview
Location: `spec/components/previews/namespace/component_name_component_preview.rb`
```ruby
class Namespace::ComponentNameComponentPreview < Lookbook::Preview
  # Default variant
  # ---------------
  # Standard component with default options
  def default
    render Namespace::ComponentNameComponent.new(param: "value")
  end
  
  # Primary variant
  # ---------------
  # Component with primary styling
  def primary
    render Namespace::ComponentNameComponent.new(
      param: "value",
      variant: :primary
    )
  end
  
  # Showcase
  # --------
  # Display all variants
  def showcase
    render_with_template
  end
end
```

### 4. Preview Template (Optional)
Location: `spec/components/previews/namespace/component_name_component_preview/showcase.html.erb`

```erb
<div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
  <%= render Namespace::ComponentNameComponent.new(
    param: "value",
    variant: :primary
  ) %>
  <%= render Namespace::ComponentNameComponent.new(
    param: "value",
    variant: :secondary
  ) %>
</div>
```
## Component Checklist
### Required Elements
- [ ] Component class extending `ApplicationComponent`
- [ ] Component template
- [ ] Lookbook preview with multiple scenarios
- [ ] RSpec component tests
- [ ] Documentation in preview comments
### Recommended Elements
- [ ] Showcase preview demonstrating all variants
- [ ] Tokyo Night color tokens usage
- [ ] Responsive design considerations
- [ ] Accessibility attributes (ARIA)
- [ ] Content slots for composition
## Code Style
### Ruby Conventions
- Use keyword arguments for parameters
- Private attr_readers for instance variables
- Helper methods for computed values
- Descriptive method names
### ERB Templates
- Semantic HTML elements
- Tailwind CSS classes
- Avoid inline styles
- Use Tokyo Night design tokens
- Proper indentation
### Preview Documentation
```ruby
# Preview title
# -------------
# Brief description of what this preview demonstrates
# @param name type "Description"
def preview_name(name: "default")
# Preview implementation
end
```
## Tokyo Night Integration
### Using Color Tokens
```ruby
include TokyoNightTokens
def background_color
TokyoNightTokens::COLORS[:bg_float]
end
```
### Tailwind Configuration
Colors available in Tailwind:
- `tokyo-blue`, `tokyo-purple`, `tokyo-cyan`
- `tokyo-green`, `tokyo-orange`, `tokyo-red`
- `tokyo-fg`, `tokyo-bg`, `tokyo-comment`
## Testing
### Component Tests
Location: `spec/components/namespace/component_name_component_spec.rb`
```ruby
require "rails_helper"
RSpec.describe Namespace::ComponentNameComponent, type: :component do
it "renders with default variant" do
render_inline(described_class.new(param: "value"))
expect(page).to have_css(".component-class")
expect(page).to have_text("Expected content")
end
it "applies variant classes" do
render_inline(described_class.new(
param: "value",
variant: :primary
))
expect(page).to have_css(".primary-class")
end
end
```
## Documentation
### Preview Comments
Document each preview scenario:
- Purpose and use case
- Parameter descriptions
- Visual differences
- Accessibility notes
### Code Comments
Focus on:
- **Why** not **what**
- Complex logic explanations
- Accessibility considerations
- Performance optimizations
- Browser compatibility notes
## Accessibility
### Required Attributes
- Semantic HTML (`<button>`, `<nav>`, `
    <article>`)
      - ARIA labels where needed
      - Keyboard navigation support
      - Focus indicators
      - Color contrast compliance
      ### Testing
      - Screen reader compatibility
      - Keyboard-only navigation
      - Focus management
      - `prefers-reduced-motion` support
      ## Performance
      ### Optimization Tips
      - Minimize DOM elements
      - Use CSS transforms for animations
      - Leverage Stimulus controllers efficiently
      - Avoid inline styles
      - Optimize asset loading
      ### Monitoring
      - Component render time
      - JavaScript execution
      - Reflow/repaint impact
      - Memory usage
